.TH MW-RECOVER 1 "2026-07-03" "MemoryWhale" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw-recover \- recover interrupted MemoryWhale session recordings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw-recover
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw-recover
scans the MemoryWhale sessions directory for recordings whose
.BR mw (1)
process was interrupted \(em by an SSH drop, a crash, or a sudden shutdown \(em
before it could write its database row, and imports those transcripts into the
local SQLite store. Already-saved sessions are left untouched. It takes no
arguments and reports what, if anything, it recovered.
.PP
The dashboard
.RB ( mw-serve (1))
runs the same recovery automatically on startup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw (1),
.BR mw-serve (1),
.BR mw-view (1)
